; CoreDNS zone for the 150-email-smtp stack — the scenario's whole mail universe.
; Publishes ONE record the edge has to be able to read: the public half of the
; throwaway DKIM key in compose.yml, at scn._domainkey.partner.example.com.
; Deliberately NO SPF and NO DMARC records — the scenario asserts both verify
; as "none", so dkim=pass alone is what authenticates partner.example.com.
$ORIGIN example.com.
$TTL 60
@                       IN SOA  ns.example.com. hostmaster.example.com. ( 1 3600 600 86400 60 )
@                       IN NS   ns.example.com.
ns                      IN A    127.0.0.1
scn._domainkey.partner  IN TXT  "v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=MIGfMA0GCSqGSIb3DQEBAQUAA4GNADCBiQKBgQDp4DSE2aJzzIkshrywfNm/OBBPrM1KAjZhN/Dn3UKfFFpKkf6w7zoL3QRNNqKHjb83pdR0+Z8ljSlV7J4Jpj/RAUFHBxTeKHeQz9WWai8bzqemJubyplmi4CEyNnzXmoAnNIwebiWcBiQ3ZNE7kte9AhdwdVWmPPaTfgbVyg3hfQIDAQAB"
